 as  anaerobe mic test panel with a  collection of clinical isolates  the micronaut panel is a standardized  growth microevolution method  performed in a 96 well microscopic plate  it contains lyophilized antibiotics and  it is suitable for both gram positives  and gram negatives  the micronut panel includes 13  antibiotics with  proven activity against anaerobes  covering all the antibiotic classes  recommended by eukast and clsi  as an example penicillins beta-lactams  plus  beta-lactamase inhibitors combinations  herbals fluoroquinolones that are  cyclists etc  each antibiotic is present in a broad  range of concentrations  most of antibiotics have eight to four  dilutions  while vacuum myosin has three and  tetracycline  s4 and they enable the determination of  mic values and their interpretation  accordingly both to eucas  or to clsi breakpoints  to inoculate a panel a modified wilkins  children growth  is used which is pre-reduced before the  use  to better support the growth also of the  most fastidious anaerobic species  now let's take a look at the study  design more in details  overall 300 not duplicate clinical  isolates were included  responding to 30 genera and 82 species  from the most common to less common ones  the strains were collected prospectively  from blood cultures  prosthetic joint infections abdominal  infections  and deep wound infections to achieve the  presence  of a higher number of different and less  common species  the number of bacteroides fragility the  most common anaerobic pathogen  was limited to the first 33 consecutive  isolates  the asd by micronaut was performed in  parallel with gradient test method  mic test strips using the same bacterial  suspensions for the inoculum of both  methods  all the procedures in this study were  performed on bench  and in air environment  the procedure to set up the test is  summarized in the pictures  from left to right briefly a 0.5  macvalen bacterial suspension  in 0.9 percent saline soluti